Subject: [PATCH 141/144] GreatDANE: allowlist branding.nsi lines and hash the
 imported preprocessor (round 4l)

Replace the NSIS command denylist with an allowlist. Logical lines
(backslash continuations joined first) of branding.nsi and its includes
must be blank, a comment, a simple !define NAME value, or a relative
sibling !include with no wildcard and no ... Anything else, including a
line starting with ${, is refused before makensis runs. Add fixtures for
the G2/G3/G4/G5/G10 denylist bypasses and for !tempfile, each with a
/tmp sentinel that must not be created.

Hash the preprocessor.py actually imported at runtime and FAIL if it
does not match the boxed ESR 153.7.0 digest. Print a separate WARN line
when makensis is the PATH 3.11 fallback.
